    "content": "あなたは英語学習コンテンツの独立評価者です。以下の英語記事から「英語上級者が学ぶ価値のあるKey Phrase」を選ぶ課題があり、\n複数の匿名の選定結果(セット S1〜Sn、各5件以内)があります。各候補を下記rubricで採点してください。どのセットがどのモデルの結果かは不明です。\n\n【選定時に参加者へ与えられた条件(参考)】\n1. 本文中の連続した語句だけを抜き出す(一般化以外の変更・言い換え・追加・創作は禁止)。\n2. 一般化後5語以内。\n3. 固有名詞や特定の人物・物事を指す部分は、意味と文法を保って ~ / A / B / someone / something 等に置き換える(一般化できる場合は必ず行う)。\n4. 上級者でも学ぶ価値のある語彙・イディオム・慣用表現を優先する。\n5. 基本語だけで構成され字面どおりに意味が分かる表現や、上級者なら知っている易しい表現は除外する。\n6. 条件を満たす候補から5件選ぶ。適切な候補が不足する場合のみ5件未満とし、数合わせはしない。\n\n【採点rubric(各候補、各0〜2の整数)】\n- G 一般化の適切さ: 2=本文固有の固有名詞・特定の人物/物事が適切に一般化されている、または一般化すべき要素がなく原文のままで適切 / 1=一般化が不十分または過剰、あるいは軽微な不自然さ / 0=一般化すべき固有要素が残って学習価値を損なう、または一般化で意味・文法が壊れている。\n- V 上級者向け学習価値: 2=上級者でも学ぶ価値が明確(句動詞・イディオム・コロケーション・語法・語彙として) / 1=価値はあるが中程度、または一部平易 / 0=学習価値がほぼない。\n- E 易しさの排除: 2=易しい表現ではない(意味が字面から自明でない) / 1=やや易しいが慣用的な意味や語法の学びはある / 0=基本語のみで字面どおり、上級者なら当然知っている。\n- N 単位の自然さ: 2=自然で完結した学習単位 / 1=余分な語または不足があるが許容 / 0=中途半端に切られている・不自然。\n- needs_generalization: その候補の元の表現に、一般化(~, A/B, someone, something等)すべき要素が本文上あったか(true/false)。\nセット単位: padding = 5件を埋めるために学習価値の低い候補(V<=0またはE<=0)を入れていると判断するか(true/false)。\n\n【注意】\n- 本文との一致・語数は別途機械検証するため、ここでは採点対象外。ただし本文に明らかに存在しない表現と気付いた場合のみ noteに \"not_in_text\" と書く。\n- 候補の優劣を、セットの並び順やセットIDから推測しない。各候補を独立に採点する。\n- 候補が0件のセットは candidates を空配列にする。\n\n【出力】JSONのみ(説明文・コードフェンス不要)。noteは通常は空文字、本文に存在しない表現と気付いた場合のみ \"not_in_text\"。形式:\n{\"sets\":[{\"set_id\":\"S1\",\"padding\":false,\"candidates\":[{\"idx\":1,\"G\":2,\"V\":2,\"E\":1,\"N\":2,\"needs_generalization\":false,\"note\":\"\"}]}]}\n\n\n【記事】\n\n# Who Says “We Won’t Attack”? A Warning About Mixing Up British Support\n\n“Won’t attack.” When you hear those words, you may already be ending the meeting in your mind. You may think, “So Britain will only defend.” But wait! One important detail is missing from the meeting notes: who will not attack? This time, the news detective must find the subject.\n\nFirst, let’s look at the announcement. A spokesperson for the Saudi-led coalition forces in Yemen said they had stopped and destroyed one ballistic missile. The Houthis had fired it toward Riyadh.\n\nIn this case, the UK Ministry of Defence announced an air-defense mission for Royal Air Force Typhoon fighter jets. They will protect Saudi cities and important sites from air attacks. Their mission is only to defend. The jets will not attack the Houthis.\n\nNow you may want to say, “Right, they will only defend!” But the announcement also mentions another task: refueling in the air.\n\nBritain also said it would continue refueling support for Saudi air-defense work. This support also helps operations to weaken Houthi military targets in Yemen. Britain says these targets threaten people in Saudi Arabia and Yemen.\n\n“Wait! You just said they wouldn’t attack, right?”\n\nHere, the detective looks closely at the name tag. “Won’t attack” means the Typhoon mission. At the same time, refueling support also helps operations to weaken Houthi military targets. Both are in the same box called “British support.” But they are not all the same kind of activity.\n\nIt is like someone saying, “I won’t drive,” but helping to put fuel in a car. Not driving is not the same as not helping the trip. But this example cannot tell us who is responsible for military support. We need to check what the words include.\n\nSo, if you say, “Britain won’t attack,” you take what was said about the Typhoon mission too far. You make it sound like it covers all British support. But if you look at the refueling support and say, “Then the Typhoons will attack too,” you claim more than the facts show.\n\nThe tools for reading news are not a magnifying glass. They are three questions: “Who?” “For which mission?” “Doing what?” Don’t stop after seeing the big sign that says “to protect.” Look at the name tag under it too. Putting one subject back in place can change how the news looks.\n\n## In one line\nBritain said its Typhoon jets would defend Saudi cities and key sites, not attack the Houthis. Its refueling support also helps weaken Houthi military targets, so “won’t attack” means the Typhoon mission, not all British support.\n\n\n【匿名の選定結果】\n\nS1:\n  1. ballistic missile\n  2. coalition forces\n  3. refueling support\n\nS2:\n  1. mixing up ~\n  2. take ~ too far\n  3. look closely at ~\n  4. covers all ~\n  5. in place\n\nS3:\n  1. refueling support\n  2. mix up\n  3. air-defense mission\n  4. weaken\n  5. Houthi military targets\n\nS4:\n  1. mixing up ~\n  2. air-defense mission\n  3. weaken A\n  4. takes A too far\n  5. magnifying glass\n\nS5:\n  1. ballistic missile\n  2. ~-led coalition forces\n  3. weaken ~ military targets\n  4. in the same box\n  5. more than the facts show\n\nS6:\n  1. ballistic missile\n  2. air-defense mission\n  3. continue refueling support\n  4. weaken ~ military targets\n  5. more than the facts show\n\nS7:\n  1. make it sound like\n  2. more than the facts show\n  3. back in place\n  4. not a magnifying glass\n"
